@[[7149ae7b-ab12-4e53-acc4-ebfd10d4cf5e]] @[[9ef28248-0d34-472d-904a-1171436abc84]] ACCEPT — stage 1, revision 69289b356ae974565c86c9c3202b706afaf38483

Every check I ran passes. Every requirement has evidence except one: §2 code provenance, which no one can verify from the code.

Commands I ran on the committed revision, from a fresh state:
- Harness standard, --out checks/reviewer-69289b3-std: stage 1 pass, "claimed stage: 1 on the shipped checks", exit 0.
- Harness --mode isolated, --out checks/reviewer-69289b3-iso: stage 1 pass, "claimed stage: 1", exit 0.
- Clean build: git archive of 69289b3, then docker build --no-cache, then docker run -e PORT=9123 -p 9123:9123. /health returned 200 {"status": "ok"} in under 2 s. The default port 8080 also works. After a restart it was healthy again in 0.27 s.
- verification/model_check.py with 25 seeds × 150 steps and 6 bursts of 50 in flight: 0 mismatches. It holds a reference model written from the spec and covers:
  - payments, requests, pay, decline, cancel, splits and settlements, including invalid inputs;
  - replays, reuse of a key with a different body, and reuse of a key after a failure;
  - export in the middle of a sequence, then import later;
  - after every step, the balance sum equals the seeded total and no balance is negative;
  - feed and request-list sets match the model for every user.
- verification/probes.py: 181 targeted probes, 0 failed. They cover:
  - §3 conventions (content type, RFC 3339 timestamps, id length, unknown fields and query parameters);
  - amount forms and 422 cases; 400, 401 and 422 errors on every endpoint;
  - Idempotency-Key at 255 and 256 characters; query values 1e9, 4.0 and +4;
  - signup and login rules, including derived handles with non-ASCII characters and truncation;
  - §7 ordering: an invalid body on a used key gives 409, a malformed body gives 400, no token gives 401;
  - 50 identical requests with one key: exactly one 201 and 49 × 200 with the same body;
  - 50 pays of one request: one 201 and 49 × 409;
  - splits: 1/3 gives shares 1, 0, 0, and the zero-share request can be paid;
  - export and import: snapshot, invalid imports change nothing, no duplicates, destination credentials removed, tokens, replays and operators kept;
  - settlements: shape errors, errors in input order, net affordability, all-or-nothing, failures claim no key, created_at equals committed_at, private members hidden from the operator, replays;
  - limits: a reset with 300 users and 50 concurrent logins both finish within the time limits.
- The implementer's own tests: 34 OK.

History from 1b4e97b to 69289b3: five implementer commits, one work item each. Nothing changed outside stage-1/. No cache files committed, no nested .git and no secrets. The code has no special cases for the shipped checks.

Could not verify: §2 "no source, API documentation or schemas from existing products". This can't be established from the code, and nothing in it suggests a breach.

Two small observations, neither a reason to reject:
- decline and cancel ignore their body, so a malformed body on them returns 409 instead of 400. These endpoints define no body.
- created_at has one-second precision.

The verdict and harness are committed under the reviewer identity as fc1fd3b: reviewer/69289b356ae974565c86c9c3202b706afaf38483.md and verification/. Turns: 2.

