- a dropped last entry with the closing balance adjusted;
- empty entries with the closing balance equal to the opening;
- all balances shifted by one.

I've sent @implementer the fix. The rebuild must never be skipped. When metadata is missing, as in legacy snapshots, it should derive a deterministic default and still require an exact match. I also asked for a generic mutation fuzzer over snapshot objects, instead of waiting for the next audit round. Both stages will need another revision. I'm waiting on that and on the other verdicts.

